<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Venda Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1898 CE (approx.) · capital Dzata</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The kingdom of the Venda in the Soutpansberg mountains, known for its sacred Lake Fundudzi and its resistance to Boer expansion.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Singo dynasty moved south across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limpopo">Limpopo</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwe plateau</a> around 1700, according to tradition, and established its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzata">Dzata</a> in the Nzhelele valley. Its rulers brought stone-walling traditions and sacred drums, and they united the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venda-people">Venda</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soutpansberg">Soutpansberg</a> under one kingship.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The king was sacred and secluded, ruling through district chiefs and councillors. Thohoyandou, remembered as the greatest ruler, is said to have vanished mysteriously. Religion centred on ancestors and sacred sites such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-fundudzi">Lake Fundudzi</a>, and the domba initiation dance became famous. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venda-people">Venda</a> traded iron and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> goods, and in 1867 they forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> settlers to abandon <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schoemansdal">Schoemansdal</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/makhado">Makhado's</a> death in 1895, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-african-republic">South African Republic</a> attacked his successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mphephu">Mphephu</a> in 1898; Mphephu fled across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limpopo">Limpopo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venda-people">Venda</a> was annexed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a>. Venda later became a nominally independent apartheid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> from 1979 to 1994.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1700 CE – 1898 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.53%;width:3.94%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1700 CE – 1898 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dzata</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Thohoyandou, Makhado, Mphephu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Venda religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tshivenda</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Singo Venda, Thohoyandou kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1799&amp;focus=venda-kingdom" aria-label="Venda Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5497 3023 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Venda Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5817 3279L5746 3380M5817 3279L5791 3172"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5746 3380h0M5791 3172h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5817 3279h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5817 3279h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dzata. <a href="/atlas?year=1799&amp;focus=venda-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
